BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI\)
CASE NO: W.P. No. 24510 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: MHC011023452026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Acting Chief Justice & Justice D. Bharatha Chakravarthy

PARTIES:
Citizens Waterbody Protection Forum
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
District Collector, Chengalpattu & Member Secretary, CMDA
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Tamil Nadu Protection of Tanks and Eviction of Encroachment Act 2007, Constitution of India

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
TN Act 8 of 2007 Section 7, Article 21, Article 48A, Article 51A\(g\)

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Water Body Protection, Encroachment Removal, Public Trust Doctrine, Ecological Balance, Wetlands

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Lake catchment area measuring 45 acres was reclassified and encroached by commercial logistics park.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Can government authorities regularize or reclassify water spread areas for industrial or commercial layouts?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
State holds all water bodies in public trust; no government authority has jurisdiction to reclassify water bodies or regularize catchment encroachments.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Writ Petition Allowed; Encroachments in lake water-spread area ordered removed within 60 days.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Acting Chief Justice & Justice D. Bharatha Chakravarthy
Madras High Court \(Principal Seat, Chennai\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
